From 96d3e60df1c56f1d62f773a99949976350e3df2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 16:15:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Netplay: one-button matchmaking, and make desktop hosts
 visible at all

Finding an opponent meant trading host codes by hand. Now there is a
single "Search for Match": it looks for a room that is open and waiting,
joins it, and if there is none it hosts one and waits to be found. Both
platforms, same rule for picking a room (one player present, not in a
game, no password) so two searchers always agree on which room wins.

The reason this could not have worked before: the desktop XD host never
published its session at all. PrepareNetplayConfig never set
NETPLAY_USE_INDEX, whose default is off, so SetupIndex bailed and every
desktop room was invisible in a lobby that was otherwise working -- the
"matchmaking is broken" complaint was a config flag. Fixed for the
manual Host button too, not just the new search.

Published rooms are named to a fixed format so people and the matcher
read the same thing. Note that the index publishes once from the server
constructor, before the game is set, so a brand-new room advertises
UNKNOWN until the next ping (~5 s) and is deliberately not matched until
then; two people searching in the very same instant can therefore both
end up hosting, which the code says out loud rather than hiding.
